{
  "_": "Entra ID (Azure) credentials read at DEPLOY TIME. Put the client secret here before deploying, and CLEAR IT AGAIN BEFORE COMMITTING \u2014 this file is tracked by git, and a secret committed once stays in the history even after it is deleted from the file.",
  "_1": "Where it comes from: Azure portal -> App registrations -> COA -> Certificates & secrets -> Client secrets. Copy the VALUE column, not the Secret ID. The value is shown only once, at creation.",
  "_2": "Leave it empty and the deployment still works: the auth stack skips the Microsoft identity provider and warns at synth. The hosted UI then shows no 'Sign in with Microsoft' button and local Cognito sign-in is unaffected.",
  "_3": "MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET in the environment takes precedence over this file, so CI can supply it without touching anything on disk.",
  "_4": "Azure client secrets EXPIRE. When this one does, Microsoft sign-in breaks with no code or infrastructure change \u2014 create a new secret in Azure, paste it here, and redeploy the auth stack.",
  "microsoftClientSecret": ""
}
